{
  "name": "onboarding asks whether the company has an office, and names the field it refuses",
  "description": "ADR-0024 decisions 11 and 17, and ADR-0017 amendment 4.\n\nOnboarding used to accept a missing address and infer nothing from it, so 'no address' could mean a fully remote company or a form nobody finished. Now the form ASKS: `workplace` is `office` or `fully_remote`, required, no default. With an office the address is compulsory — country, city and street, postcode and second line optional as before. Fully remote, none is given, and one sent anyway is REFUSED rather than silently stripped; an address object whose every part is empty counts as not sent, because that is what a form with disabled fields submits (RFC-0024 §2).\n\nEvery refusal on both routes is `422 {\"error\": \"invalid_onboarding\", \"field\": …}`, replacing the `invalid_claim` a bare ErrInvalid used to fall through to — a company told its CLAIM was rejected, in a contributor's noun. `field` is the path in the request, so the address's parts are `address.country`, `address.city` and `address.street1`, and the first missing part is the one named. All ten rows of the table are run on POST /organizations and again on POST /organizations/revise, each request wrong in one way only; none of them writes a submission.\n\nApproval is keyed on the choice, not on a blank: the office company gets exactly one address, its main office, written with the organisation and the owner seat; the fully remote one gets none. `organizations.workplace` is copied from the submission, and the admin queue shows `workplace`, with `address` null exactly when it is fully_remote. A rejected company revising may change its answer, since a revision is a whole new submission (ADR-0017 §8).\n\nAmendment 1 §1.9: revising checks the form first and the code second, and a refused form does NOT spend the code — so the ten refused revisions below all present the same code, and the corrected eleventh, with that same code, is accepted.",
  "seed": ["principals"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "POST /organizations — no name.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/organizations",
        "body": {
          "email": "refused-name-0@example.test",
          "workplace": "fully_remote"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_onboarding",
          "field": "name"
        }
      }
    },
    {
